And a module-level mechanism:

```python
class _Updater:
    def __init__(self):
        self._in_progress = False
        self._changed = []  # cells whose value changed during the update
        self._previous = {}  # cell -> value before update

    def begin(self):
        self._in_progress = True

    def finish(self):
        self._in_progress = False
        for cell in self._changed:
            if cell._value != self._previous[id(cell)]:  # hmm
                for cb in cell._callbacks:
                    cb(cell._value)
        self._changed = []
        self._previous = {}
```

